            <ArticleTitle>Immunosurveillance of Malignant Cells with Complex Karyotypes.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>880-884</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0962-8924(17)30159-9</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.tcb.2017.09.001</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A wide array of cell-intrinsic surveillance mechanisms maintains the homeostasis of dividing cells and the integrity of the genome. Accumulating evidence also supports a role for cell-extrinsic mechanisms. Among them, the immune system, together with cell-autonomous checkpoint processes, eliminates cells that harbor unbalanced karyotypes generated by mitotic defects.</AbstractText>
